V. CONCLUSION
The Purdue Model remains a foundational architecture for securing industrial environments by enforcing strict separation between IT and OT systems. Through layered segmentation, dedicated monitoring tools, and adherence to industrial cybersecurity standards, organizations such as Caterpillar, Komatsu, and John Deere can reduce cyber risk and improve operational resilience. As cyber-physical systems evolve and manufacturing environments become increasingly connected, adopting the Purdue Model with modern SOC tools, OT monitoring platforms, and packet-level analysis techniques such as Wireshark will be essential for maintaining secure and reliable industrial operations.
